{"kind":"field","id":"R0043","key":"partition_assignment","status":"OBSERVED","finding":"Fine-grained fused-block partitioning (DIA-FP) groups consecutive convolutional layers into fusion blocks b_n and spatially partitions them into sub-blocks b_{ni} with receptive-field kernel overlap; many-to-many offloading (DIA-O) assigns sub-tasks from each user UAV to up to theta server UAVs via overlapping coalition formation.","locators":[{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0043.pdf","page":2,"section":"II.B DNN Model","quote":"the fused block b_n can also be partitioned into sub-fused blocks such as b_n = {b_{n1}, b_{n2}, ..., b_{ni}}"},{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0043.pdf","page":4,"section":"III.B Offloading Strategy Based on DIA-O","quote":"Each user node will offload fine-grained partitioned DNN tasks to multiple server nodes"}],"gap":null}
{"kind":"field","id":"R0043","key":"optimization","status":"OBSERVED","finding":"Decision variables: fusion-block partition scheme P_k and binary user-server offloading matrix X = [x_{s,u}]. Objective: minimize total inference time sum (T_{sa}^{tr} + T_{sa}^{exe} + T_{sa}^{que}) and min-max coalition utility Upsilon(CS). Constraints: 1 <= sum x_{s,u} <= theta and SINR >= Gamma. Solver: two-stage decomposition using greedy iterative fusion partitioning (DIA-FP, Algorithm 1) and a genetic-algorithm overlapping coalition formation solver (DIA-O).","locators":[{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0043.pdf","page":3,"section":"II.C Problem Definition and Analysis","quote":"min sum_{s in S} sum_{a in A} T_{sa} . x_{s,a}"},{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0043.pdf","page":4,"section":"III.B Offloading Strategy Based on DIA-O","quote":"We propose an overlapping coalition formation algorithm based on genetic algorithm to obtain the optimal matching scheme."}],"gap":null}
