{"kind":"field","id":"R0064","key":"architecture","status":"OBSERVED","finding":"Air-ground collaborative inference system with M UAVs (M=2 or 3), N=50 ground PoIs, and K=2 fixed ground edge servers (ESs); UAVs host a compressed DNN model for local inference while ESs host the uncompressed DNN model and share bandwidth/compute equally among associated UAVs.","locators":[{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0064.pdf","page":3,"section":"3. System model and problem formulation","quote":"we consider a multi-UAV video surveillance system that consists of M UAVs, N PoIs and K ESs."},{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0064.pdf","page":3,"section":"3. System model and problem formulation","quote":"the compressed DNN model is deployed on UAVs to reduce computational complexity. The uncompressed DNN model is deployed at ESs."}],"gap":null}
{"kind":"field","id":"R0064","key":"workload","status":"OBSERVED","finding":"Multi-frame video recognition (e.g., gesture/action recognition) at fixed 1080x1080 resolution with selectable frame counts I=[5,6,7,8,9,10,11,12,13,15,17,20]; inference accuracy is modeled analytically via G_m(i_m(t))=-g_1/(i_m(t)+g_2)+g_3 (g_1=0.707, g_2=0.939, g_3=0.990) with a 5% compressed-model accuracy loss rather than executing a named DNN on a video dataset.","locators":[{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0064.pdf","page":8,"section":"5.1. Simulation setup","quote":"the input size of one video frame is 1080×1080 pixels."},{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0064.pdf","page":8,"section":"5.1. Simulation setup","quote":"the set of optional video frame number is set as I = [5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 15, 17, 20]."}],"gap":null}
{"kind":"field","id":"R0064","key":"partition_assignment","status":"OBSERVED","finding":"Binary full-task offloading per time slot (o_{m,k}(t) in {0,1}, sum_{k=0}^K o_{m,k}(t)=1): each UAV either executes its multi-frame video task locally on its compressed DNN (k=0) or offloads all sampled frames to one ES (k in 1..K) for uncompressed DNN inference (partial offloading excluded due to temporal correlation).","locators":[{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0064.pdf","page":5,"section":"3.3. Computation offloading","quote":"we consider the binary offloading manner, i.e., each UAV can either execute the DNN inference task locally or offload the task to one of the ESs."}],"gap":null}
{"kind":"field","id":"R0064","key":"optimization","status":"OBSERVED","finding":"Decision variables: continuous 3D UAV flight (v_m^h, theta_m^h, v_m^v), discrete frame count i_m(t), binary offloading o_{m,k}(t). Objective: minimize average inference delay (1/TM) sum tau_m(t). Constraints: 3D area/height bounds, D_min=50 m separation, accuracy >= A_th (0.9), every PoI monitored >=1 time per frame, energy <= E_max (25 KJ). Solver: cooperative MAPPO-HA (multi-agent hybrid-action PPO with multi-branch Tanh/Softplus/Softmax actor and GAE).","locators":[{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0064.pdf","page":6,"section":"3.5. Problem formulation","quote":"P1: min_{Q, I, O} (1/T)(1/M) sum_{t=1}^T sum_{m=1}^M tau_m(t)"},{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0064.pdf","page":7,"section":"4.2. MAPPO-HA algorithm","quote":"the proposed MAPPO-HA algorithm integrates the processing mechanisms of MAPPO for discrete and continuous actions, to solve the hybrid action space without approximation or relaxation."}],"gap":null}
