{"kind":"field","id":"R0075","key":"partition_assignment","status":"OBSERVED","finding":"Offline teacher-channel ranking by validation activation strength s_c and deterministic partitioning across UAVs by compute capability with rho=0.2 boundary overlap (212 unique -> 238 assigned channels); online, each UAV dynamically picks an early exit k_i in {2,3,4} (k_min=2) supporting mixed-depth fusion at the Master.","locators":[{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0075.pdf","page":4,"section":"III.C Offline Training: Multi-Exit Feature Alignment","quote":"The teacher channels are ranked according to s_c and then partitioned across student models according to the onboard computational capability of their corresponding UAVs."},{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0075.pdf","page":4,"section":"III.C Offline Training: Multi-Exit Feature Alignment","quote":"The main model uses overlap ratio rho = 0.2, yielding 212 unique teacher channels and 238 assigned channels after overlap."}],"gap":null}
{"kind":"field","id":"R0075","key":"optimization","status":"OBSERVED","finding":"Online binary exit/continue routing decision a_{i,k} in {a_exit, a_cont} for k >= k_min. Objective: maximize team reward r_t = I(y_hat=y) - lambda * D_t / D_scale where D_cc = max{d_{0,k_0}^{comp}, max_i(d_{i,k_i}^{comp} + B_{i,k_i}/R_i)}. Solver: validation-learned, test-frozen Master-Sequential LinUCB heuristic using 7D context vectors and ridge-regression UCB updates (default lambda=0.35).","locators":[{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0075.pdf","page":7,"section":"III.D.4 Reward Design and Policy Update","quote":"r_t = I(y_hat = y) - lambda D_t / D_scale"},{"source":"restart_2026_11_26/fulltext_retrieval/pdf/R0075.pdf","page":3,"section":"I. INTRODUCTION","quote":"We develop a validation-learned, test-frozen LinUCB-inspired sequential routing heuristic."}],"gap":null}
